---
// src/pages/share/kevin-christensen-vetting/sources.astro
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Sources — Did Serving Our Country Count Against Kevin Christensen? — Skovgard 2026"
  description="Public sources supporting the Kevin Christensen candidate-vetting message: his military record, the Candidate Vetting Committee correspondence, Wyoming Statute 22-25-104, and the Wyoming GOP's federal lawsuit."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-20">

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <div class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-3 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest">
        <a href="/share" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">All messages</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <a href="/share/kevin-christensen-vetting" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">Kevin Christensen</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <span class="text-wy-charcoal">Sources</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="bg-wy-charcoal py-14 px-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3">Research Notes</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-extrabold text-wy-bone mb-4 leading-tight">
        Kevin Christensen and the 2026 Candidate Vetting Process
      </h1>
      <p class="text-wy-bone/70 text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto">
        Sources supporting the claims in the share message.
        This is a research aid, not a legal opinion.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Preamble -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl px-6 py-5 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>About this page.</strong> The correspondence supplied for review says the
            Candidate Vetting Committee intended to recommend that Kevin Christensen not receive
            an endorsement at that time. Kevin submitted a response. The party's executive
            director acknowledged it and said it had been provided to the committee. The supplied
            record does not contain a final endorsement decision — this page describes the
            recommendation as <strong>preliminary</strong> throughout.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Important limitation.</strong> The vetting-notice and response correspondence
            (dated July 17&#8211;18, 2026) is a campaign-held document — email sent directly to
            statewide candidates. It has not been independently published online, so no public
            link is available for it below. It is described here from the original document, with
            private phone numbers and campaign staff email addresses omitted.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main content -->
    <article class="bg-wy-bone py-12 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto sources-content">

        <!-- Core issue -->
        <h2>Core issue</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          The message asks whether a candidate-vetting process that weighs donations, party
          organizational involvement, and registration history can fairly account for a candidate
          whose adult life was spent in active-duty military and federal service &#8212; where
          ordinary partisan activity is often limited by duty itself. It rests on Kevin
          Christensen&#8217;s documented military record, the committee&#8217;s own stated
          criteria, and the current state of Wyoming law restricting party spending in primary
          elections.
        </p>

        <!-- Wyoming law -->
        <h2>Wyoming law at issue</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The relevant statute is <strong>W.S. 22-25-104</strong>, titled
          <em>Restriction on party funds in primary elections</em>.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="statute-block">
          "No political party funds shall be expended directly or indirectly in the aid of the
          nomination of any one person as against another person of the same political party
          running in the primary election."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          W.S. 22-25-104 &#8212; Wyoming Legislature, Title 22, page 183.
        </p>

        <!-- Timeline -->
        <h2>Public timeline and context</h2>
        <div class="timeline-list mb-10">
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <span class="timeline-date">March 19, 2026</span>
            <p>
              Wyoming Public Media reported Kevin Christensen&#8217;s U.S. House campaign
              announcement, independently confirming a nearly three-decade military career, two
              Bronze Star Medals, the Legion of Merit, the Valorous Unit Award for Task Force
              Gunslinger, and service on the Joint Staff advising senior military and civilian
              leaders.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <span class="timeline-date">June 4, 2026</span>
            <p>
              WyoFile and Cowboy State Daily reported that the Wyoming Republican Party filed a
              federal lawsuit challenging W.S. 22-25-104, seeking authority to spend party money
              on guides ranking and expressly endorsing candidates before the primary.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <span class="timeline-date">July 17&#8211;18, 2026</span>
            <p>
              Email correspondence supplied by Kevin Christensen: a Candidate Vetting Committee
              notice listing questionnaire responses, past party donations, prior party
              attendance and involvement, registration history, legislative voting records, and
              outside support as criteria, followed by Kevin&#8217;s response citing 100%
              alignment with the party platform and asking how criteria beyond the party&#8217;s
              own bylaws (Article II, Sections 13.1&#8211;13.4) are authorized and applied.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Claims table -->
        <h2>Key claims and source support</h2>
        <div class="claims-table" role="table" aria-label="Claims and source support">
          <div class="claims-header" role="row">
            <span role="columnheader">Public claim</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Best source</span>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              Kevin Christensen served more than 27 years in the Army, including combat
              leadership in Iraq, command at company/battalion/brigade levels, and service on
              the Joint Staff at the Pentagon.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Christensen campaign biography; independently confirmed by Wyoming Public Media
              (two Bronze Star Medals, the Legion of Merit, the Valorous Unit Award).
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              The Candidate Vetting Committee intended to recommend withholding endorsement at
              this time, and weighs donations, party attendance/involvement, registration
              history, and legislative scorecards.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Email correspondence supplied by Kevin Christensen, July 17&#8211;18, 2026.
              Campaign-held document; not published online.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              Kevin has no legislative voting record to score, since his career was military and
              federal service, not elected office.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Same July 17&#8211;18, 2026 correspondence; consistent with his campaign biography
              showing no prior elected office.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              Wyoming law restricts party funds from aiding one same-party primary candidate over
              another.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              W.S. 22-25-104, Wyoming Legislature Title 22 PDF.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              Party leadership has challenged that restriction in federal court; a final ruling
              is still pending.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              WyoFile and Cowboy State Daily reporting on the June 4, 2026 lawsuit filing.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              The available record does not contain a final endorsement decision &#8212; only a
              preliminary recommendation and confirmation it was sent to the committee for review.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Same July 17&#8211;18, 2026 correspondence. No further documentation has been
              supplied establishing a final decision.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Source list -->
        <h2>Primary sources</h2>

        <div class="source-list">

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Candidate Vetting Committee notice and Kevin Christensen&#8217;s response
              <span class="source-desc">Campaign-held document — not published online</span>
            </p>
            <span class="source-link todo-link">
              No public link available — email correspondence dated July 17&#8211;18, 2026,
              supplied by Kevin Christensen
            </span>
            <p class="source-note">
              Notice lists questionnaire responses, past party donations, prior party attendance
              and involvement, registration history, legislative voting records, outside support,
              and other criteria. Kevin&#8217;s response states 100% alignment with the party
              platform and asks how criteria beyond Article II, Sections 13.1&#8211;13.4 are
              authorized and applied. Private phone numbers and campaign staff email addresses
              are intentionally omitted from this public page.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Christensen for Wyoming — Meet Kevin
              <span class="source-desc">Campaign biography — military record</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.christensen2026.org/meet-kevin"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              christensen2026.org — Meet Kevin
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Reports more than 27 years of military service, service as an AH-64 Apache pilot,
              command at company, battalion, and brigade levels, combat leadership in Iraq, the
              rank of colonel, and work as a senior adviser and division chief on the Joint Staff
              at the Pentagon.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Wyoming Public Media — Military vet Kevin Christensen announces U.S. House run
              <span class="source-desc">Independent Wyoming news report — military record</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.wyomingpublicmedia.org/politics-government/2026-03-19/military-vet-kevin-christensen-announces-u-s-house-run"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyomingpublicmedia.org — Kevin Christensen announces U.S. House run
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Independently reports a nearly three-decade military career, two Bronze Star
              Medals, the Legion of Merit, the Valorous Unit Award for Task Force Gunslinger, and
              service on the Joint Staff advising senior military and civilian leaders.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Wyoming Legislature: Title 22 PDF
              <span class="source-desc">Official state statutes source — W.S. 22-25-104</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title22.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov — Title 22 PDF
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Official source for W.S. 22-25-104, the statute restricting party funds in primary
              elections. Statute text appears on page 183 of Title 22.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              WyoFile — Wyoming GOP sues state, challenges constitutionality of ban on pre-primary candidate endorsements
              <span class="source-desc">Independent Wyoming news report — federal lawsuit challenging W.S. 22-25-104</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://wyofile.com/wyoming-gop-sues-state-challenges-constitutionality-of-ban-on-pre-primary-candidate-endorsements/"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyofile.com — Wyoming GOP sues state
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Reports the June 4, 2026 federal lawsuit and accurately distinguishes an
              endorsement statement from the statute&#8217;s restriction on the expenditure of
              party funds.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Cowboy State Daily — Wyoming GOP sues state for right to back most-aligned Republicans
              <span class="source-desc">Independent Wyoming news report — federal lawsuit</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://cowboystatedaily.com/2026/06/04/wyoming-gop-sues-state-for-right-to-back-most-aligned-republicans/"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              cowboystatedaily.com — Wyoming GOP sues state
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Reports that the lawsuit asks a federal court to declare the restriction
              unconstitutional and block its enforcement. The existence of the lawsuit does not
              itself suspend the statute — the legal question belongs to the court.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Apache Warrior — U.S. Army Aviation documentary
              <span class="source-desc">Image credit — background photography used in the share image</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3Pgg__jYco"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              youtube.com — Apache Warrior documentary
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Source of the AH-64 Apache and aircrew photography used in the share message&#8217;s
              image. Documentary footage, not a personal photograph of Kevin Christensen&#8217;s
              own unit or deployment.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- Notes for responsible use -->
        <h2>Notes for responsible use</h2>
        <ul class="responsible-list">
          <li>The committee&#8217;s recommendation is described in the supplied record as preliminary. Do not describe it as a final denial of endorsement — the record does not establish a final decision.</li>
          <li>W.S. 22-25-104 is a statute, not a court ruling. Describe it as Wyoming law restricting party funds — not as a ruling on the pending lawsuit.</li>
          <li>The federal lawsuit is pending. Describe the party&#8217;s legal challenge as a filed complaint, not a resolved question &#8212; the statute remains in force unless and until a court says otherwise.</li>
          <li>The July 17&#8211;18, 2026 correspondence is a private, campaign-held communication. Do not represent it as a public document, and omit personal contact information in any further use.</li>
          <li>The available record does not establish the committee&#8217;s motives or how each criterion was weighted. Those questions require additional documentation this packet does not have.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Back CTA -->
    <div class="bg-white py-12 px-4 border-t border-gray-200 text-center">
      <a href="/share/kevin-christensen-vetting"
         class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-wy-ember text-wy-bone font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to the message
      </a>
    </div>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .sources-content { line-height: 1.75; color: #2b2b2b; }
  .sources-content h2 {
    font-family: 'Bitter', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #c68a4a;
  }
  .sources-content h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .statute-block {
    background: #fefce8;
    border-left: 4px solid #c68a4a;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Timeline */
  .timeline-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid #c68a4a;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-left: 8px;
  }
  .timeline-item {
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .timeline-item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -27px;
    top: 6px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #c68a4a;
    border: 2px solid #f1ece1;
  }
  .timeline-item:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .timeline-date {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #c68a4a;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .timeline-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Claims table */
  .claims-table {
    border: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .claims-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    background: #2b2b2b;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .claims-header span {
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #f1ece1;
  }
  .claims-header span:first-child { border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
  .claims-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
  }
  .claims-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .claims-row div {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2b2b2b;
  }
  .claims-row div:first-child {
    background: #f1ece1;
    border-right: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .claims-row div:last-child { background: #fafaf8; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .claims-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-header span:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
    .claims-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-row div:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce; }
  }

  /* Source list */
  .source-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e2da;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .source-item {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e2da;
  }
  .source-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .source-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #0f2742;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .source-desc {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
  }
  .source-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #b22234;
    text-decoration: none;
    word-break: break-all;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .source-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .todo-link {
    color: #6b7280;
    font-style: italic;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .source-note {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Responsible use */
  .responsible-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .responsible-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .responsible-list li::before {
    content: "•";
    color: #c68a4a;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
</style>
